media: i2c: dw9719: fix probe error on surface go 2

On surface go 2, sometimes probing dw9719 fails with
"dw9719: probe of i2c-INT347A:00-VCM failed with error -121".
The -121 (-EREMOTEIO) comes from i2c-designware-common.c and indicates
the initialize happens too early, so just add a delay. There is no exact
reason for 10000us, but 100us failed.

NOT OURS - this is linux-surface's own patch (author: mojyack), carried in
linux-surface/patches/6.19/0013-cameras.patch. It is reproduced here only
because the out-of-tree module in src/dw9719/ replaces the built-in
dw9719.ko wholesale and therefore has to contain it too.

If you are building against a linux-surface kernel tree, this hunk is
already applied - use 0001 alone.

Applies to : linux v6.19.x, drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
Apply with : patch -p1 < 0002-...patch     (run from the kernel tree root)

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
@@ -121,6 +121,9 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Wait for device to be acknowledged */
+	fsleep(10000);
+
 	/*
